body:
Well, it looks like classfile annotations are pickled as well.

`class W extends scala.annotation.ClassfileAnnotation; @W trait X`

Decompilation shows:

```
@ScalaSignature(bytes="\006\001M1q!\001\002\021\002G\005QAA\001Y\025\005\031\021a\002\037f[B$\030PP\002\001'\t\001a\001\005\002\b\0315\t\001B\003\002\n\025\005!A.\0318h\025\005Y\021\001\0026bm\006L!!\004\005\003\r=\023'.Z2uQ\t\001q\002\005\002\021#5\t!!\003\002\023\005\t\tq\013")
public abstract interface X
{
}
```

Note there are no java annotations on X, so all the info is to be stored in the pickle.

